# Optional overrides — unifi-network-mcp has no required env vars.
# Authentication is per-request via headers (provided by the MCP caller):
#   X-Unifi-Host       The customer's UniFi controller host, reachable from
#                       wherever this server runs — bare host/IP or a full
#                       https:// URL, with or without a port (normalized
#                       internally). This is a self-hosted, per-customer
#                       controller — there is no shared/cloud default.
#                       IMPORTANT: this server calls the controller directly,
#                       so it only works if the controller is reachable from
#                       here — for a cloud-hosted gateway that means the
#                       customer has exposed their local controller's API to
#                       the internet (their own choice/risk — see README).
#   X-Unifi-Api-Key     The local API key generated on that controller
#                       (Settings > Control Plane > Integrations > API Keys).
#                       Do not use the customer's admin username/password —
#                       the local API key is a dedicated, revocable
#                       credential and is the only auth this server accepts.
#   X-Unifi-Verify-Ssl  Optional, defaults to "true". Set to "false" only if
#                       the controller presents a self-signed certificate —
#                       discouraged, since the request is now going over the
#                       public internet (not a LAN), so skipping TLS
#                       verification has real MITM exposure. Prefer putting a
#                       valid cert on whatever the customer exposes instead.
#
# This server calls the controller's official Network Integration API
# directly with these per-request credentials — it has no shared/brokerable
# auth layer to delegate to a gateway, and never persists credentials beyond
# one request.

MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
